This fork was vendored from the PUBLISHED, BUNDLED NPM ARTIFACT
(dist/index.js, dist/index.d.ts, and the other dist/ and src/*.css files
listed in package.json's "files" array), not from the upstream TypeScript
source tree. The upstream source repository
(github.com/microsoft/vscode-packages, directory
vscode-team-tools/packages/markdown-editor) was not reachable from the
execution environment that produced this fork (cross-owner repository
attach was unavailable), and the npm tarball itself ships only the built
dist/ output plus a handful of CSS files under src/ — no TypeScript source.

This is recorded as a deliberate, documented deviation from the ideal of
forking from source, with an explicit follow-up: regenerate this fork from
the upstream TypeScript source once the source repository is reachable, or
upstream the renderCustomBlock seam itself as a pull request against
microsoft/vscode-packages so this fork becomes unnecessary. See
docs/plans/source-first-editor/runs/SFE-P1b.md ("Provenance constraint") and
PATCHES.md ("Upstreaming / removal trigger") for the full record. This fork
is designed for deletion per CLAUDE.md's design-for-deletion rule: it exists
only to carry one missing generic extension seam and should be removed the
moment upstream provides an equivalent, or Chrome/VS Code make it moot.

Everything under dist/ and src/ in this package is Microsoft's published,
MIT-licensed work, byte-identical to the published tarball except for the
minimal, clearly marked ("/* gp-fork: renderCustomBlock */") additive patch
documented in PATCHES.md. No Gutterpress-specific syntax, vocabulary, or
branding has been introduced into the fork itself.
